  "body": "Currently pipeTo takes a second options argument, which can be { close: false } to turn off automatically closing the writable stream when the readable stream is exhausted.\n\nProposed improvements:\n- [ ] Switch the boolean, so that false is the default, as is best practice for APIs that accept booleans. I think { preventClose: true } would be the new one.\n- [ ] Add a way of controlling whether we abort the dest if the source errors. { preventAbort: true }\n- [ ] Add a way of controlling whether we cancel the source if the dest errors. { preventCancel: true }\n\nI think these names don't need to be super-explicit since they are for advanced use cases that people will read the documentation for anyway. So that is why for example I am not too concerned about potential confusion between preventAbort and preventCancel.\n\nWDYT?\n",
